GUARDIANA for Windows\par
\par
GUARDIANA shows you which services your AI talks to and, with Home Mode, every device on your Wi-Fi: it explains each one in a sentence and blocks only what you decide. Everything happens on this PC. No account, no server of ours, zero telemetry.\par
\par
What this installer will do\par
- Copy the program to \u8220?Program Files\\Guardiana\u8221?.\par
- Register the \u8220?Guardiana\u8221? service, which starts with Windows.\par
- Add the \u8220?Guardiana\u8221? shortcut, which opens the panel in your browser, to the Start menu and the desktop, and the \u8220?Guardiana (menu)\u8221? shortcut to the Start menu.\par
- Make GUARDIANA this PC's DNS, over IPv6 too, so it starts watching from the first minute. It first keeps an exact copy of your setting; if the service stops, the PC gets its previous DNS back, and uninstalling leaves it exactly as it was.\par
\par
What it will NOT do\par
- It does not read what you send or receive: only the service name, the time and the device.\par
- It opens no port to the network. Only Home Mode, when you turn it on, opens ports on your home Wi-Fi; turning it off closes them.\par
\par
After installing\par
The panel opens when the installer finishes and within a minute you will see this PC's queries. To put the DNS back as it was without uninstalling: panel, \u8220?Status\u8221?. Blocking one specific name works from the first minute; broad blocks, by category or for the whole home, wait until GUARDIANA has been watching that device for 24 hours.\par
\par
Seven days with every feature, no card needed; after that you need a licence (a subscription or a single payment). What was written down stays on your disk, whether you pay or not.\par
\par
Program licence: GNU GPL 3.0 or later. Open source: you can read it, build it and check that it does what it says. What GUARDIANA does not do is in WHAT_IT_DOES_NOT_DO.md, in the published source code (github.com/guardianagroup/guardiana).\par
